# PRIMES-ENUM  -  prime-number enumerator for the Busch Microtronic 2090
#
# Displays the primes 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, ... in decimal, one after another,
# pausing after each, then HALTs after the last prime below 1000 (997).
#
# Just LOAD and RUN (no input needed) -- unlike the interactive PRIMES.MIC,
# this one simply counts up and shows every prime it finds.
#
# Method: trial division by the built-in DIV, using DIV's remainder flag
# and its quotient (for a sqrt(n) early-out).  See PRIMES-ENUM.asm for the
# fully commented source.
#
# Delay length is tunable: the word at address 39 is  '3'  (the high nibble
# 3 of instruction 13C = 'MOVI 3,C').  Raise it (up to F) for a longer pause
# between numbers, lower it for a shorter one.
# Each unit is about one second on the real machine (the pause is roughly 3 s as shipped).
#
# Registers: R8/R9/RA = n (units/tens/hundreds), R6/R7 = trial divisor,
#            RC/RD/RE = delay counters.  (c) source: CC BY 4.0.

